    "client_msg_id": "924f36de-8d80-49de-97ea-c5c537665ee7",
    "text": "■ 現状\n```% dig +short polimoney.dd2030.org -t CAA\n6b104dc31631b0da.vercel-dns-017.com.\n0 issue \"sectigo.com\"\n0 issue \"globalsign.com\"\n0 issue \"letsencrypt.org\"\n0 issue \"pki.goog\"```\n> If any Certification Authority Authorization (CAA) domain record exists on the root domain, you must explicitly allow DigiCert as a certificate issuer by creating a CAA domain record with the value 0 issue <http://digicert.com|digicert.com>. Without this setting, the certificate issuance and renewal fail. \n> <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/container-apps/custom-domains-managed-certificates?pivots=azure-portal>\nとあるので、\n```polimoney.dd2030.org. IN CAA 0 issue \"digicert.com\" ```\nが必要なのかなと思いましたがどうなんでしょう？",
